---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Turning Missed Deadlines Into Proactive Alerts - Marker">
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-24 md:pb-24">
      <a
        href="/case-studies"
        class="mb-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground"
      >
        <svg
          class="mr-1 h-4 w-4"
          fill="none"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
        >
          <path
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
        </svg>
        All Case Studies
      </a>

      <span
        class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-primary"
      >
        Lifestyle Apparel
      </span>
      <h1
        class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl"
      >
        Turning Missed Deadlines Into Proactive Alerts
      </h1>

      <div
        class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm"
      >
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Company</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground"
              >Lifestyle apparel brand, wholesale + DTC</span
            >
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Team</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground"
              >Supply chain team managing a calendar-driven product-to-market
              process</span
            >
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Key Challenge</span
            >
            <span class="text-muted-foreground"
              >No visibility into why deadlines were missed or what the downstream
              impacts were</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Challenge</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          The interim head of supply chain at this lifestyle apparel brand — a
          veteran with 25 years of experience at a major American fashion house —
          put the core problem plainly: "Nobody knows that they miss deadlines
          and what the impacts are."
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          The team's product-to-market process was organized around a calendar of
          major milestones, but when deadlines slipped, there was no systematic
          way to understand why. Email threads on a single topic routinely grew
          to 50 or more messages. Digging through those threads to reconstruct
          what happened — and when — was painful and time-consuming.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          The result was that "hindsighting" — understanding the root cause of
          delays so the team could prevent them in future seasons — was nearly
          impossible. Without a central record tying communication history to
          milestone performance, every post-mortem required manual detective
          work. Onboarding new suppliers was equally difficult, since process
          knowledge lived in individual inboxes rather than in any shared system.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Marker uses the team's product calendar as the organizing principle for
          all supplier communication. Each email, message, and file exchange is
          automatically linked to the relevant milestone — whether that's a
          prototype submission, lab dip approval, or final shipment date.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          When a milestone is at risk, Marker surfaces the relevant
          communications and highlights where delays originated. Rather than
          scrolling through 50-message email chains, the supply chain lead can
          see an AI-generated summary at the top of each thread, organized by the
          key decisions and dates discussed.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          This same data powers hindsighting at the end of each season. The team
          can answer questions like "Why were we late on this delivery?" by
          tracing back through the communication timeline tied to that milestone.
          For supplier onboarding, Marker also serves as a living process
          reference — new suppliers and new team members can see how the workflow
          is actually executed, not just how it's documented on paper.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-muted-foreground">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Calendar-driven organization links every supplier communication
              to the relevant product milestone</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >AI-generated summaries at the top of long email threads reduce
              time spent reconstructing conversation history</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Hindsighting becomes data-driven: the team can trace delays back
              to specific communications and handoff points</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Proactive alerts when milestones are at risk, based on
              communication patterns and response timelines</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Supplier onboarding simplified through a shared process
              reference built from actual communication history</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section
        class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-6 text-center"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">
          See how Marker can give your team visibility into deadline performance.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/book-demo"
          class="mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2"
        >
          Book a Demo
        </a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
